        "title": "Progress of application and off-target effects of CRISPR/Cas9.",
        "id": "https://openalex.org/W1862162016",
        "cited_by_count": 10
      },
      "description": "These articles center on CRISPR-Cas9 genome engineering with a particular emphasis on off-target activity as a major barrier to accurate and safe editing. Collectively, they review or analyze the mechanistic basis of unintended cleavage, compare methods for detecting and predicting off-target sites, and discuss strategies to improve specificity, from high-fidelity Cas variants and sgRNA design tools to experimental mitigation in pooled screening settings. The inclusion of temperature effects fits this theme as a practical parameter influencing Cas9 editing efficiency and specificity, highlighting how editing outcomes depend on both molecular design and experimental conditions."
    },
