        "id": "https://openalex.org/W2001799395",
        "cited_by_count": 4
      },
      "description": "This cluster centers on the safety and specificity of CRISPR-Cas genome editing, with particular attention to unintended DNA changes that can arise either at off-target genomic sites or unexpectedly at the intended target locus. The articles combine genome-wide detection and validation methods with strategy-oriented reviews, using tools such as Digenome-seq, sequencing-based genotyping, and other assay platforms to map cleavage errors, quantify on-target damage, and evaluate ways to minimize or eliminate these side effects in research and therapeutic applications."
