        "title": "Achieving Plant CRISPR Targeting that Limits Off‐Target Effects",
        "id": "https://openalex.org/W2527347512",
        "cited_by_count": 94
      },
      "description": "These papers center on the deployment of CRISPR/Cas9 as a genome-engineering platform across animals and especially plants, with a shared focus on making editing efficient, heritable, and precise for trait generation or functional studies. Methodologically, they combine zygote or embryo injection, donor-mediated knock-in, multiplex targeting, and viral or plant-compatible delivery systems, while also explicitly evaluating and reducing off-target mutations through improved guide design and Cas9 variants. Together, they capture the push to turn CRISPR into a reliable, high-specificity tool for practical genome modification in model organisms and crops."
    },
